 "about": "Paths as they are written and the names they are read into, for the core (src/pathtext.rs) and the app to read alike. paths: text is a path as written; tree is the name before an @ written before the sections (main@Store:Order, of before; absent when none); sections are the sections' names from the top (before the :, or the whole of a path with a / and no :); colon is whether a : was written (absent: false); names are the names after the : (or of a path with neither : nor /), the card's first; picks, when present, says for each name what is written inside its [...] (\"\" for [], null for none; absent: none for every name); written is the path as it is kept, each name quoted only when it needs it (absent: the same as text); refused instead says why the path cannot be read (empty, unclosedQuote, stray, emptyName, unclosedBracket, bracketInSection). names: name is a name; written is how it is written in a path; problem, when present, is why it cannot be a name (empty, tooLong, control, spaces). A name is quoted when it holds whitespace or one of / : . [ ] ' @ | { } # \" ` and a ' inside is doubled; a pick's key is quoted as a name is, and also when it holds = or ,. refs: text is a piece of Markdown; refs are the references the scanner finds in it, in order, each with its kind (place, value, embed), path, and shown (a place's |text) and option (an embed's |option) when present; renamed, when present, is the text again with each reference to from naming to instead (the shown text kept). sectionOnly: text is a path; section is the sections it names when it names a section alone (a : with nothing after it), null when it does not.",
